                    </p>

                </article>


                <article class="r154-gameday-report-card">

                    <span class="r154-gameday-report-label">
                        Follow-Up
                    </span>

                    <h3>
                        Preserve Relevant Information
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Retain the game card, notes, MatchTrak information and
                        any requested documentation until referee leadership
                        confirms the matter is complete.
                    </p>

                </article>

            </div>


            <div class="r154-gameday-report-warning">

                <strong>
                    Do not publish or assume one permanent card-drop location.
                </strong>

                Until the field-specific process is confirmed, ask the Center
                Referee, Field Marshal or Region representative where the
                completed card must be delivered.

            </div>


            <div class="r154-gameday-backlink-wrap">

                <a class="r154-gameday-backlink" href="#page-menu">
                    Back to Game Day Tools Menu
                </a>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- ================================================================
             SAFETY AND SUPPORT
             ================================================================ -->

        <section class="r154-gameday-section r154-gameday-section-alt" id="safety-support" aria-labelledby="safety-support-title">

            <div class="r154-gameday-protection-panel">

                <span class="r154-gameday-eyebrow">
                    Referee Safety Comes First
                </span>

                <h2 id="safety-support-title">
                    Referee Protection and Game-Day Escalation
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Referees must not be threatened, intimidated, insulted or
                    aggressively confronted before, during or after a match.
                    Concerns about decisions must be handled through the
                    approved Region process.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Youth referees require immediate adult protection and
                    should never be expected to manage an aggressive adult
                    without support.
                </p>


                <div class="r154-gameday-protection-highlight">

                    When an interaction becomes unsafe, stop the confrontation,
                    remain with the referee crew and seek a Field Marshal or
                    Region representative.

                </div>


                <div class="r154-gameday-protection-steps">

                    <div class="r154-gameday-protection-step">

                        <span class="r154-gameday-protection-number">
                            1. Do Not Debate
                        </span>

                        Avoid an extended argument with a coach, player or
                        spectator.

                    </div>


                    <div class="r154-gameday-protection-step">

                        <span class="r154-gameday-protection-number">
                            2. Notify the Crew
                        </span>

                        Tell the Center Referee or another experienced official.

                    </div>


                    <div class="r154-gameday-protection-step">

                        <span class="r154-gameday-protection-number">
                            3. Seek Region Support
                        </span>

                        Contact the Field Marshal or Region representative.

                    </div>


                    <div class="r154-gameday-protection-step">

                        <span class="r154-gameday-protection-number">
                            4. Report the Event
                        </span>

                        Notify referee leadership and complete the required
                        report.

                    </div>

                </div>


                <div class="r154-gameday-protection-actions">

                    <a class="r154-gameday-button r154-gameday-button-red" href="/Default.aspx?tabid=974653">
                        Referee Abuse Prevention
                    </a>

